// `__array_new__` with an i64 fill. The refusal's stated reason is STALE: it reads "No i64[] /
// f32[] backing exists yet (only i32/f64/string/ref lists), so an i64 / f32 fill would
// otherwise store into the i32 backing" — but `i64[]` and `f32[]` lists both lower and run
// today (`nulScalarListWrapHeap` maps `nuli64list` to `il64TypeIdx`), so the backing the
// comment says is missing is present. Whether the intrinsic can simply use it is unmeasured;
// what is measured is that the reason given no longer holds.
// A clause-2 violation by construction: `vl check` returns 0 and the EMITTER refuses.
// Found 2026-09-01 with D958's phrase-list audit.
// Should print 2.
const v: i64 = 7

const xs = __array_new__(2, v)

print(xs.length)
